Conversio: do not double Retina display dimensions again in GetDeviceCaps.

CrossOver 26.3 win32u's null DC driver already gets HORZRES/VERTRES from the
display rectangle/system metrics populated by winemac. With Retina enabled,
those are already physical dimensions. The extra winemac shift reports
6912x4468 for a 3456x2234 display, while EnumDisplaySettings and DXGI report
3456x2234. Unity 2019 then requests an impossible fullscreen mode and its UI
can be cropped. Preserve physical millimetres and all other forwarded caps.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
@@ -218,10 +218,9 @@
     default:
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&device_data_mutex);
         dev = GET_NEXT_PHYSDEV( dev, pGetDeviceCaps );
-        ret = dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
-        if ((cap == HORZRES || cap == VERTRES) && retina_on)
-            ret *= 2;
-        return ret;
+        /* win32u already uses the display rectangle, including Retina scaling.
+         * Multiplying it again disagrees with EnumDisplaySettings and DXGI. */
+        return dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
     }
 
     TRACE("cap %d -> %d\n", cap, ret);
